            <title>[LU-21171] ofd: lock_zero_regions() reads past the FIEMAP reply when fm_extent_count is 0</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21171</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name="Problem"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Problem&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;On a kernel with KASAN, sanity test_44f fails with "Error in dmesg detected". The OSS log has:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;BUG: KASAN: slab-out-of-bounds in lock_zero_regions+0x706 [ofd]
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It is an 8-byte read just past the end of a 600-byte reply buffer. The buffer was allocated by null_alloc_rs(), from ofd_get_info_hdl() -&amp;gt; req_capsule_server_pack(), in an ll_ost thread. Without KASAN the test passes, because nothing checks the read.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name="Cause"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Cause&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;multiop's do_fiemap() (the "I" command in test_44f) first sends a count-only probe: fm_extent_count = 0 with FIEMAP_FLAG_SYNC. With FIEMAP_FLAG_SYNC the client sets OBD_FL_SRVLOCK.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In ofd_get_info_hdl() (KEY_FIEMAP):&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The reply is sized from fm_extent_count, so it only holds the struct fiemap header (no extents).&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;ofd_fiemap_get() sets fm_mapped_extents to the real number of extents, as FIEMAP does for a count-only call.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Because OBD_FL_SRVLOCK is set (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-3219" title="FIEMAP does not sync data or return cached pages" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-3219"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-3219&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;), lock_zero_regions() runs. It loops "i &amp;lt; fiemap-&amp;gt;fm_mapped_extents" and reads fm_extents&lt;span class="error"&gt;&amp;#91;i&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;.fe_logical, which is past the end of the reply.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;


&lt;p&gt;The values read are also used as lock ranges, so the locked regions are wrong too.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name="Possiblefix"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Possible fix&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Only walk the extents that are in the buffer:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="code panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="codeContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre class="code-java"&gt;&lt;span class="code-keyword"&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; (i = 0; i &amp;lt; min(fiemap-&amp;gt;fm_mapped_extents, fiemap-&amp;gt;fm_extent_count); i++) {
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With fm_extent_count = 0 the loop is skipped and [fm_start, fm_start + fm_length) is locked once, which is what a count-only query with SYNC needs.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name="Environment"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Environment&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Found on a 2.17.57-based build, single node, Rocky 9.8 debug kernel (5.14.0-687 with KASAN, lockdep and debug objects). lock_zero_regions() and the FIEMAP handler are the same in master (2.17.61).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name="Related"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Related&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19463" title="usercopy failure with CONFIG_HARDENED_USERCOPY" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-19463"&gt;LU-19463&lt;/a&gt;: the same 44f probe (fm_extent_count = 0) causes a usercopy failure on the client. This ticket is the server side.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-17110" title="Slab corruption using fiemap ioctl with fm_extent_count==0" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-17110"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-17110&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;: client slab corruption with fm_extent_count = 0 (resolved).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
</description>
